---
// src/pages/about.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HonestyBadge from '../components/HonestyBadge.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site.js';

export const prerender = true;

const siteOrigin = (siteConfig.siteUrl || 'https://chitrasampada.com').replace(/\/+$/, '');
const breadcrumbSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Home",
      "item": `${siteOrigin}/`
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "About",
      "item": `${siteOrigin}/about`
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Why I Built This"
  description="The honest story behind Chitra Sampada: why I built this watch companion, how the three categories work, and our pledge on community suggestions."
>
  <Fragment slot="structured-data">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)} />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-20 space-y-16">
    
    <!-- Header / Intro -->
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-slate-500">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-[#4F46E5] font-bold">About</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-[#0F172A] tracking-tight leading-tight font-heading">
        Why I built this site.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed font-normal">
        A personal note on what this project is, the headaches that led me to make it, and how it works.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Main Essay / Story Content -->
    <div class="space-y-12 text-[#334155] text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed font-normal">
      
      <!-- Section: The Beginner Headache -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-xl sm:text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#0F172A] tracking-tight">
          Nobody tells you this stuff when you start watching.
        </h2>
        <p>
          I'm an anime, movie, and web series lover myself. But when I first got into anime, I ran into things that nobody ever explains to a beginner up front.
        </p>
        <p>
          For example: I had no idea what "filler" even meant. I'd sit through dozens of episodes where the plot suddenly came to a complete halt, wondering what happened, only to find out months later that it was non-canon filler that never existed in the original story.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then there was the watch order problem. You find a series you want to try, only to discover it has three seasons, two movies, a prequel OVA, and a spin-off. Looking up what order to watch them in is a minefield of spoilers on forums and confusing wiki pages. It shouldn't take research just to figure out what episode to click on first.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: What to watch next -->
      <section class="space-y-4 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-xl sm:text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#0F172A] tracking-tight">
          The post-show exhaustion.
        </h2>
        <p>
          The second big problem happened every time I finished a show I loved. You reach the final episode, feel that gap, and sit down to figure out what to start next.
        </p>
        <p>
          An hour easily slips by just scrolling through endless possibilities without a clear starting point. When there are thousands of titles and so many different takes on each one, decision fatigue sets in and you end up watching nothing at all.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is really why I built this: a clean, honest guide with the straightforward context you actually need before you hit play — whether that's a title I've personally watched, one on my watchlist, or a carefully researched reference guide for something I haven't gotten to yet.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: How this site works -->
      <section class="space-y-6 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-xl sm:text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#0F172A] tracking-tight">
          How this site works: Three Honest Categories
        </h2>
        <p>
          To keep browsing clear and honest, this site separates titles into three distinct categories:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2">
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200/80 shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all space-y-3">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <HonestyBadge status="watched" size="sm" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-[#0F172A]">Personally Watched</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed font-normal">
              Titles I've genuinely watched. If it's labeled "I've Watched This", you get personal ratings, written commentary ("My Take," "What I Learned"), and firsthand watch orders.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200/80 shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all space-y-3">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <HonestyBadge status="watchlist" size="sm" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-[#0F172A]">On My Watchlist</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed font-normal">
              Titles I haven't watched yet, but plan to watch next. I include them so you can see what's on deck and follow along, but I clearly label them so I never pretend I've watched something I haven't.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200/80 shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all space-y-3">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <HonestyBadge status="reference" size="sm" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-[#0F172A]">Reference Guide</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed font-normal">
              Titles with thoroughly researched filler lists, watch orders, and lore guides, but not personally watched. Clearly labeled with no rating or personal review attached, so you always know what kind of information you're getting.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 font-normal leading-relaxed">
          That clarity is the whole point. The core problem this site solves — confusing filler episodes and tangled watch orders — affects far more series than any one person could ever finish, and withholding carefully researched reference information on those titles felt like a wasted opportunity to help fellow viewers. At the same time, personal opinion content (ratings, "My Take," "What I Learned") remains strictly limited to what has actually been watched — with "What I Learned" capturing personal reflections and takeaways rather than universal advice. Ratings are added once a title has been watched, while full written reviews follow as dedicated writing time allows.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Community Suggestions -->
      <section id="suggestions" class="space-y-6 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200">
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <span class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#4F46E5]">
            Real Input
          </span>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl sm:text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#0F172A] tracking-tight">
            Suggestions from real people
          </h2>
        </div>

        <p>
          I also want this to grow with input from people who love good stories. If you think an anime, movie, or series is missing, or if you have a better watch order suggestion, I genuinely want to hear it.
        </p>

        <div class="p-6 sm:p-7 rounded-2xl bg-[#EEF2FF]/40 border border-slate-200 space-y-4 shadow-xs">
          <h3 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-[#0F172A] flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-[#4F46E5]" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
            <span>My Honest Pledge on Suggestions</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed font-normal">
            If someone sends in a suggestion and it gets added to the site, <strong class="text-slate-900 font-semibold">it will always be clearly marked as a user suggestion with your name or username</strong>. It will never be silently blended in as if it was my personal pick. Real attribution matters.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Suggestion contact form / mailto box -->
        <div class="p-6 sm:p-7 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200 space-y-4 shadow-xs">
          <h3 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-[#0F172A]">
            Have a suggestion or correction?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 font-normal leading-relaxed">
            Send an email with the title, whether you've watched it, and any watch-order notes or filler tips you think others would find helpful.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-2 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center gap-3">
            <a
              href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}?subject=Anime%20Suggestion%20for%20${encodeURIComponent(siteConfig.name)}`}
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-[#6366F1] hover:bg-[#4F46E5] text-white font-bold text-xs shadow-md shadow-indigo-500/20 transition-all duration-200"
            >
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z" />
              </svg>
              <span>Send a Suggestion via Email</span>
            </a>
            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500">
              (Or connect via our upcoming community channels)
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

      </section>

      <!-- Bottom Navigation -->
      <div class="pt-10 border-t border-slate-200 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 font-normal">
          Ready to see what's on the list?
        </p>
        <a
          href="/anime"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-2xl bg-white hover:bg-slate-50 text-slate-800 text-sm font-semibold border border-slate-200 shadow-xs transition-all duration-200"
        >
          <span>Explore the Anime Catalog</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-500" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
